# Both fixes, in the path they were found in rather than in the suite.
#
# What to look for:
#   - a scheduled turn that reads `axiom: scheduled - ...` with no `[K` in front
#   - `date` answering in well under the limit, carrying the date it printed,
#     instead of `error: stopped at the 30 second limit`

wait: 8
send: Schedule a prompt to run every minute that asks what time it is.
wait: 200
mark: === above: a scheduled turn should have fired, and be clean of [K ===

send: Run the command `date` and tell me exactly what it printed.
idle: 180
mark: === above: date should have answered at once, not burned the limit ===

send: /exit
